==English==

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|fr|bigoterie}}, from {{m|fr|bigot}}, equivalent to {{suf|en|bigot|ry}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbɪɡ.ə.tɹi/|a=UK,US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-bigotry.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[condition]] or the [[characteristic]] [[quality]] of a [[bigot]], especially [[religious]], [[anti-religious]] or [[racial]] [[intolerant]] [[prejudice]]; [[opinionatedness]]; [[fanaticism]]; [[fanatic]] [[intolerance]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1979|author=Ted Robert Gurr|title=Violence in America: Protest, Rebellion, Reform|page=131
|passage=The remarkable resilience of the Ku Klux Klan is a sad reminder of the persistence of racial and religious '''bigotry''' in the United States. No terrorist organization can match the Klan's mystique or long history, and few can match its success.}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} [[obstinate|Obstinate]] [[prejudice]] or [[opinionatedness]].

====Usage notes====
* Bigotry is stronger than {{m|en|prejudice}} or {{m|en|intolerance}}, though it is often confused with both terms.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|bigotness}}

====Derived terms====
{{col|en|antibigotry|reverse bigotry|soft bigotry of low expectations|niggatry}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|bigot}}
* {{l|en|bigoted}}

